<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Nested signable items, kept separate from the main app's file.

    electron-builder applies this to every nested Mach-O it signs, not just the
    four helper .app bundles: verified on the shipped 0.1.24 bundle, the same
    entitlements had landed on node-pty's spawn-helper and on @vscode/ripgrep's
    rg. A ripgrep binary was signed with disable-library-validation because one
    file served both roles.

    allow-jit is here for the Renderer and GPU helpers, which run V8 and Skia.
    It is inert on spawn-helper, on rg, and on the .node and .dylib payloads,
    none of which JIT and none of which need an entitlement to load once they
    carry this app's own team signature.

    Anything the harness process turns out to need belongs in
    entitlements.mac.plist instead. The harness child IS the main binary, so
    there is never a reason to widen this file to reach it.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
